  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — `canon/web`\n\n**Zero test infrastructure exists.** No test runner is installed (no Jest/Vitest in `package.json`), no config file, and no `*.test.ts(x)` files anywhere in the repo. Every gap below is therefore \"untested,\" but I've prioritized by risk since you can't fix all of it at once.\n\n**Recommended setup first** (blocks everything else):\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react jsdom @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom @testing-library/user-event\n```\nAdd to `package.json`: `\"test\": \"vitest run\"`, `\"test:watch\": \"vitest\"`. Vitest over Jest — this is an ESM/TS-native Next.js 16 + React 19 project, and Vitest avoids the transform config pain Jest needs here.\n\n---\n\n### Priority 1 — Pure logic, zero excuse not to test (`lib/format.ts`, `lib/reviewer-label.ts`, `types/rules.ts`, `types/run.ts`)\n\nThese have no I/O, no mocking needed, and are exercised on every page render.\n\n**`lib/format.ts`** — 7 exported functions, 0 tests.\n\nEdge cases missed:\n- `shortRunId`: id shorter than 6 chars after stripping hyphens (partial/empty result), id with no hyphens, id that's already short\n- `formatElapsed`: negative ms (clamped to 0?), ms that lands exactly on 60s/3600s boundaries, values >24h\n- `formatCount` / `formatStat`: negative numbers, `0` vs `null` vs `undefined` (the whole point of `formatStat` — it must never confuse 0 with unset)\n- `formatRelative`: boundary at exactly 60s/60m/24h, a `date` in the future relative to `now` (negative seconds)\n- `formatConfidence`: values outside 0–1 (e.g., `1` → `\"1.00\"`, does it round correctly at `0.005`)\n\n```ts\n// lib/format.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  shortRunId, formatElapsed, formatCount, formatStat,\n  formatClockTime, formatTimestamp, formatRelative, formatConfidence,\n} from \"@/lib/format\";\n\ndescribe(\"shortRunId\", () => {\n  it(\"takes 4 chars, ·, 2 chars from a hyphenated uuid\", () => {\n    expect(shortRunId(\"a41fbc21-c9aa-4444-8888-000000000000\")).toBe(\"a41f·bc\");\n  });\n  it(\"handles an id shorter than 6 chars after stripping hyphens\", () => {\n    expect(shortRunId(\"ab-cd\")).toBe(\"abcd·\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it(\"clamps negative ms to 00:00\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(-500)).toBe(\"00:00\");\n  });\n  it(\"switches to h:mm:ss past one hour\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(3_600_000)).toBe(\"1:00:00\");\n  });\n  it(\"stays mm:ss just under one hour\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(3_599_000)).toBe(\"59:59\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"renders 0 as '0', not an em dash\", () => {\n    expect(formatStat(0)).toBe(\"0\");\n  });\n  it(\"renders null/undefined as an em dash\", () => {\n    expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(\"—\");\n    expect(formatStat(undefined)).toBe(\"—\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  it(\"says 'just now' under 60s\", () => {\n    const now = new Date(\"2026-08-06T12:00:00Z\");\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-06T11:59:30Z\"), now)).toBe(\"just now\");\n  });\n  it(\"rolls over at exact minute/hour/day boundaries\", () => {\n    const now = new Date(\"2026-08-06T12:00:00Z\");\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-06T11:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"60m ago\"); // or 1h — verify intended rounding\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it(\"always shows two decimals\", () => {\n    expect(formatConfidence(1)).toBe(\"1.00\");\n    expect(formatConfidence(0)).toBe(\"0.00\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/reviewer-label.ts`** — the audit trail's display identity resolution, untested:\n\n```ts\n// lib/reviewer-label.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewerLabel } from \"@/lib/reviewer-label\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j.rao\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to email when username is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j@x.com\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to the userId when user is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to userId when both username and email are missing\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: null }, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"treats empty-string username as falsy? (verify: '' ?? is truthy in JS)\", () => {\n    // NB: `??` only falls through on null/undefined, so username: \"\" would return \"\".\n    // This is worth a dedicated test to lock in current (possibly surprising) behavior.\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"\", primaryEmailAddress: null }, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n```\nThat last case is a genuine edge case worth locking down either way — `??` doesn't treat `\"\"` as absent, so a Clerk user with an empty-string username (if that's ever possible) would render blank instead of falling back.\n\n**`types/rules.ts`** — `orderRulesByEvaluation` / `ruleSpecificity` implement the survivorship rule-priority contract described in the file's own comment (\"first match wins\"). This is exactly the kind of ordering logic that silently breaks on refactor and has no test today.\n\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { orderRulesByEvaluation, ruleSpecificity, type SurvivorshipRule } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\nconst rule = (overrides: Partial<SurvivorshipRule>): SurvivorshipRule => ({\n  id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\", ...overrides,\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"scores exact field + exact entityType highest\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(rule({ field: \"name\", entityType: \"account\" }))).toBe(3);\n  });\n  it(\"scores double wildcard lowest\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(rule({ field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" }))).toBe(0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"orderRulesByEvaluation\", () => {\n  it(\"sorts most specific first\", () => {\n    const wildcard = rule({ id: \"wild\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" });\n    const specific = rule({ id: \"specific\", field: \"name\", entityType: \"account\" });\n    expect(orderRulesByEvaluation([wildcard, specific]).map((r) => r.id)).toEqual([\"specific\", \"wild\"]);\n  });\n  it(\"keeps author order among equal-specificity rules (stable sort, first match wins)\", () => {\n    const a = rule({ id: \"a\", field: \"name\", entityType: \"*\" });\n    const b = rule({ id: \"b\", field: \"phone\", entityType: \"*\" });\n    expect(orderRulesByEvaluation([a, b]).map((r) => r.id)).toEqual([\"a\", \"b\"]);\n  });\n  it(\"does not mutate the input array\", () => {\n    const input = [rule({ id: \"a\" }), rule({ id: \"b\", field: \"x\" })];\n    const copy = [...input];\n    orderRulesByEvaluation(input);\n    expect(input).toEqual(copy);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`types/run.ts`** — `isTerminalRunStatus`, `runStageIndex`:\n\n```ts\n// types/run.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { isTerminalRunStatus, runStageIndex } from \"@/types/run\";\n\ndescribe(\"isTerminalRunStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"complete and failed are terminal\", () => {\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"complete\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"every in-progress stage is non-terminal\", () => {\n    for (const s of [\"queued\", \"extracting\", \"matching\", \"detecting\", \"resolving\"] as const) {\n      expect(isTerminalRunStatus(s)).toBe(false);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runStageIndex\", () => {\n  it(\"returns -1 for failed (carries no position, per the doc comment)\", () => {\n    expect(runStageIndex(\"failed\")).to